---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ScreenGallery from '../components/ScreenGallery.astro';
import AppGrid from '../components/AppGrid.astro';
import RatingChart from '../components/RatingChart.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Overview"
  banner={true}
  intro="An internal reference library for the SCB Easy overhaul. Research artefacts are rendered straight from source, so the library is never out of step with them."
>
  <h2 id="about-scb">About us</h2>
  <p>
    Siam Commercial Bank was established by royal charter on 30 January 1906 as the first
    Thai bank. It operates today as a universal bank serving retail, SME and corporate
    customers, with an international presence across Cambodia, China, Myanmar, Vietnam,
    Singapore and Laos, and subsidiaries including SCB Securities and SCB Asset Management.
  </p>
  <p>
    Retail services span home loans, personal credit, car hire purchase, cards, currency
    exchange, remittances, investment and insurance. Corporate and SME services cover cash
    management, lending, trade finance, treasury, capital markets and advisory.
  </p>
  <p>
    The bank's stated strategic direction is <em>SCB Transformation</em>, which prioritises
    digital channels, organisational agility, data analytics capability, and ecosystem links
    between consumers and entrepreneurs.
  </p>
  <p class="src">
    Summarised from <a href="https://www.scb.co.th/en/about-us.html">scb.co.th/en/about-us</a
    >. That page is the source of truth; this is a précis and may lag it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="about-scb-easy">About SCB Easy</h2>
  <p>
    SCB Easy is the bank's retail mobile banking app and its primary consumer digital
    channel. SCB retired its SCB Easy Net internet banking service, making the app the main
    route for self-service retail banking.
  </p>

  <ScreenGallery slug="scb-easy" />

  <p>Its published feature set covers four areas:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Money movement</strong> — fee-free domestic transfers to any Thai bank, bill
      payment by QR or provider, and top-ups for mobile credit, tolls, e-wallets and prepaid
      cards.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Account access</strong> — account management, transaction history, and
      cardless ATM withdrawal with no transaction fee.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Financial products</strong> — WEALTH4U investment advisory, EASY-D debenture
      accounts, and the SCB Gold Marketplace.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lifestyle and security</strong> — "Just for You" personalisation, "Easy Bonus"
      offers, and Easy Security. Registration is by facial recognition, SCB ATM, or branch.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="src">
    Summarised from <a
      href="https://www.scb.co.th/en/personal-banking/digital-banking/scb-easy.html"
      >scb.co.th · SCB Easy</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sister-apps">Sister apps</h2>
  <p>
    The nine consumer apps in the SCBX portfolio, across three business pillars. Install
    counts and ratings are store-reported as at 16 September 2026 and move continuously.
  </p>

  <AppGrid />

  <RatingChart />

  <p class="src">
    Portfolio data and screens come from the SCBX Screen Estate inventory. See <a
      href="/studies/STU-001_scb-easy-benchmark-desk-research/inputs/documents/scbx-screen-estate"
      >the artefact</a
    > for coverage limits — 110 of its 145 screens are storefront creatives rather than interface.
  </p>

  <style>
    .src {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--s-text-helper);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
